 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nParser fails to handle STRUCT type with identifier that is also a type token\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing SQL with STRUCT types that contain identifiers which are also type tokens (like `list` in `STRUCT<list ARRAY<...>>`), the parser incorrectly handles the identifier, causing parsing failures.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should parse successfully but fails\nsql = \"CAST(x AS STRUCT<list ARRAY<INT64>>)\"\ntry:\n    result = sqlglot.parse_one(sql)\n    print(\"Parsed successfully:\", result)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Parse failed:\", e)\n\n# Similar issue with other type tokens used as identifiers\nsql2 = \"CREATE TABLE x (a STRUCT<values ARRAY<INT64>>)\"\ntry:\n    result = sqlglot.parse_one(sql2)\n    print(\"Parsed successfully:\", result)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Parse failed:\", e)\n```\n\nThe parser should be able to handle cases where identifiers in STRUCT definitions happen to be type tokens like `list`, `values`, etc.\n</issue>\n",
